    "lawCode": "Amd §92-a, Pub Serv L; amd Part H1 §4, Chap 62 of 2003",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9305A\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to restructuring the\nNew York telecommunications relay service center as a workforce employ-\ning residents of Onondaga county or adjoining counties; and to amend\nchapter 62 of the laws of 2003, amending the public service law relating\nto establishing the New York telecommunications relay service center, in\nrelation to extending certain provisions thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis will extend the provisions of law establishing the New York tele-\ncommunications relay service workforce until June 30, 2030.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection One: Amends the public service law relating to establishing the\nNew York telecommunications relay service workforce to extend its under-\nlying authorization.\n\nSection Two - Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPublic Service Law section 92-a(2)(a) requires that the New York Tele-\ncommunications Relay Service workforce be located in Syracuse, New York.\n\nThis provision expires on June 1, 2027. This legislation extends this\nprovision until June 30, 2030.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
